      "content": "it doesn't even feel like grief anymore. grief implies there's something to mourn, but i just feel... hollow. like the light went out and the room is just dark now. i go through the motions, i eat, i sleep, but i'm just a ghost in this place. i don't see the point in trying to reconstruct a person who doesn't even exist.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
